00:45:52,620 --> 00:46:22,140
By 1965, the project was only two-thirds occupied, with that population level still falling. Vacancies were distributed pretty evenly. That is, every building and every floor still had some number of occupants, so you couldn't really downsize maintenance by mothballing some buildings. So they started to defer maintenance, right? So trash began to pile up in front of the incinerators, hallways weren't cleaned, safety patrols were cut.

98
00:46:22,880 --> 00:46:49,660
Elevators broke and were never fixed. Light fixtures were replaced with new vandal-proof light fixtures, both more difficult and more expensive to replace, and more tempting for would-be vandals. Windows were broken and went unreplaced for weeks at a time. The place started to fall apart, and anyone who could get out of the project started trying to get out of the project.

